\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Zero-temperature phases for $n=4$. (a) Channel space with $\kappa _3=-1$, $\kappa _4=0$, from direct minimization (colors) and exact boundaries (black): T--F, Eq.~\eqref  {eq:TF} (solid), D--F, Eq.~\eqref  {eq:DF} (dashed), and C--D, Eq.~\eqref  {eq:CD} (dotted). U$^\prime $ is an umbrella variant of U. (b) Physical plane at $J=1$, $K=0.5$ with T--C (solid), T--F (dashed), and C--F (dotted) boundaries of Table~\ref {tab:phases}. (c) Sketches of the cluster states; $\times k$ marks $k$ coincident spins.}}{4}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:T0}{{2}{4}{Zero-temperature phases for $n=4$. (a) Channel space with $\kappa _3=-1$, $\kappa _4=0$, from direct minimization (colors) and exact boundaries (black): T--F, Eq.~\eqref {eq:TF} (solid), D--F, Eq.~\eqref {eq:DF} (dashed), and C--D, Eq.~\eqref {eq:CD} (dotted). U$^\prime $ is an umbrella variant of U. (b) Physical plane at $J=1$, $K=0.5$ with T--C (solid), T--F (dashed), and C--F (dotted) boundaries of Table~\ref {tab:phases}. (c) Sketches of the cluster states; $\times k$ marks $k$ coincident spins}{figure.2}{}}
