\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Channel selection at finite temperature, from the individual runs. (a) Cut E$^\prime $: the nematic temperature $T_2$ (red) does not depend on the odd-channel coupling $zG$, while the D-phase ordering temperature $T_1$ (green) does. Circles: 2D, $L=16$ (open) and $24$ (filled); squares: 3D, $L=8$ (open) and $10$ (filled); diamonds: 3D $L=12$, where the ladder (0.8--1.2\,$T_1$) does not reach $T_2$. Error bars are jackknife errors of the susceptibility peaks. Dashed (2D) and dotted (3D) lines: $T_1\propto G M^2$ normalized at $zG=1$. (b) Cut E: $T_1$ of the D order in a preliminary $L=8$ trial with ordered start (squares) and the same scaling; the C state at $zG=0.5$ shows no order. Cut D: $T_2$ from the specific-heat peak of heating and cooling ladders ($L=16$, triangles) and an $L=8$ trial (circles).}}{8}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:channel}{{6}{8}{Channel selection at finite temperature, from the individual runs. (a) Cut E$^\prime $: the nematic temperature $T_2$ (red) does not depend on the odd-channel coupling $zG$, while the D-phase ordering temperature $T_1$ (green) does. Circles: 2D, $L=16$ (open) and $24$ (filled); squares: 3D, $L=8$ (open) and $10$ (filled); diamonds: 3D $L=12$, where the ladder (0.8--1.2\,$T_1$) does not reach $T_2$. Error bars are jackknife errors of the susceptibility peaks. Dashed (2D) and dotted (3D) lines: $T_1\propto G M^2$ normalized at $zG=1$. (b) Cut E: $T_1$ of the D order in a preliminary $L=8$ trial with ordered start (squares) and the same scaling; the C state at $zG=0.5$ shows no order. Cut D: $T_2$ from the specific-heat peak of heating and cooling ladders ($L=16$, triangles) and an $L=8$ trial (circles)}{figure.6}{}}
