\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Phases near the ferro--nematic line (2D, $K=0.5$, $zH_4=1.5$). Thin colored lines: harmonic plus label predictions for F$|$M2 and M2$|$C. Black line and band: fit $zG^*=1+aT+bT^2$; black symbols: the individual slab zero crossings (dots: input to the fit; open diamonds: rescan of $T=0.175$ and $0.20$ with a larger range, auxiliary). Gray lines: label-only and harmonic-only slopes. At $zG=1.1$: wedge boundaries $T_1$ (F$|$M2, purple) and $T_2$ (M2$|$C, red) from slab coexistence in 2D (open circles) and 3D (squares) with their errors, and the thermodynamic-integration predictions ($\times $).}}{9}{figure.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:H6}{{7}{9}{Phases near the ferro--nematic line (2D, $K=0.5$, $zH_4=1.5$). Thin colored lines: harmonic plus label predictions for F$|$M2 and M2$|$C. Black line and band: fit $zG^*=1+aT+bT^2$; black symbols: the individual slab zero crossings (dots: input to the fit; open diamonds: rescan of $T=0.175$ and $0.20$ with a larger range, auxiliary). Gray lines: label-only and harmonic-only slopes. At $zG=1.1$: wedge boundaries $T_1$ (F$|$M2, purple) and $T_2$ (M2$|$C, red) from slab coexistence in 2D (open circles) and 3D (squares) with their errors, and the thermodynamic-integration predictions ($\times $)}{figure.7}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces (a) Effective specific-heat exponent $a=d\ln C_{\max }/d\ln N$ for every pair of sizes $L_0\to L_1$, with 16--84\% errors from the block-jackknife errors of $C_{\max }$: the octupolar ($l=3$) transition of the tetrahedral phase in 3D (filled circles) and 2D (open squares), and the 2D nematic ($l=2$) transition at $zH_4=2$ (triangle). The band marks standard 3D continuous transitions and the dashed line first-order scaling. (b) $T_c$ of the first-order 3D nematic transition ($zH_4=1$) from slab coexistence at two slab sizes; the latent heat is from window chains.}}{9}{figure.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:order}{{8}{9}{(a) Effective specific-heat exponent $a=d\ln C_{\max }/d\ln N$ for every pair of sizes $L_0\to L_1$, with 16--84\% errors from the block-jackknife errors of $C_{\max }$: the octupolar ($l=3$) transition of the tetrahedral phase in 3D (filled circles) and 2D (open squares), and the 2D nematic ($l=2$) transition at $zH_4=2$ (triangle). The band marks standard 3D continuous transitions and the dashed line first-order scaling. (b) $T_c$ of the first-order 3D nematic transition ($zH_4=1$) from slab coexistence at two slab sizes; the latent heat is from window chains}{figure.8}{}}
